Tension: guard OgreFreeImageCodec2.cpp on OGRE_NO_FREEIMAGE
============================================================

Why this patch exists
---------------------
OGRE-Next's OgreMain/CMakeLists.txt:403 unconditionally seeds

    set( BROKEN_FILES_IN_UNITY_BUILD "src/OgreFreeImageCodec2.cpp" )

and CMake/Utils/OgreAddTargets.cmake:55 then does

    set(_SOURCES ${_PRIMARY} ${_EXCLUDES})

i.e. the SEPARATE list is *appended* to the target's sources, not subtracted
from them. The `if (OGRE_CONFIG_ENABLE_FREEIMAGE)` block at
OgreMain/CMakeLists.txt:354 only adds the header, source and FreeImage_LIBRARIES
when the option is ON; it never removes anything when it is OFF.

So `-DOGRE_CONFIG_ENABLE_FREEIMAGE=OFF` clears only the codec *registration*.
The translation unit is still compiled, and it does

    #include <FreeImage.h>          // OgreFreeImageCodec2.cpp:48

with no `#if OGRE_NO_FREEIMAGE` guard anywhere in its 705 lines. Disabling the
codec therefore fails the build:

    OgreMain/src/OgreFreeImageCodec2.cpp:48:10: fatal error:
      FreeImage.h: No such file or directory

(on a machine that still has the header it fails at link instead).

This patch adds the guard the file should have had: the whole translation unit
compiles to an empty object when OGRE_NO_FREEIMAGE is set, so OGRE can be
configured without FreeImage and without patching CMake.

Placement is load-bearing
-------------------------
`#if !OGRE_NO_FREEIMAGE` must sit *after* `#include "OgreStableHeaders.h"`.
The macro is defined by OgreConfig.h (OgreMain/include/OgreConfig.h:169-170,
reached through OgreStableHeaders.h), so a guard at line 1 sees it undefined —
the preprocessor reads that as 0, `!0` is true, and the file compiles anyway.
Measured: a line-1 guard moved the same error from :48 to :49.

Upstream state
--------------
Unfixed as of ogre-next master (pinned here at 475f783d76). If upstream adds
the guard, this patch becomes a no-op (patch -N --forward reports "previously
applied" and skips); if upstream changes the surrounding lines, bootstrap.mjs
fails loudly with the rejected hunk rather than silently skipping.

Source
------
Measured in this repo's FreeImage-removal experiment (2026-11-06) against the
pinned submodule: OgreNextMain and the full tree build, and
`ldd lib/libOgreNextMain.so` lists no libfreeimage.

Applied by scripts/bootstrap.mjs after the submodule checkout. It is never
edited in place by hand: AGENTS.md rule 1 keeps third_party/ogre-next read-only,
and the build is supposed to reproduce through `npm run bootstrap`.

--- a/OgreMain/src/OgreFreeImageCodec2.cpp
+++ b/OgreMain/src/OgreFreeImageCodec2.cpp
@@ -28,6 +28,11 @@
 
 #include "OgreStableHeaders.h"
 
+// Tension: honour OGRE_NO_FREEIMAGE so this TU compiles to nothing when the
+// codec is disabled. OgreConfig.h, via OgreStableHeaders.h above, defines it;
+// the guard must therefore follow that include and not precede it.
+#if !OGRE_NO_FREEIMAGE
+
 #include "OgreFreeImageCodec2.h"
 
 #include "OgreDataStream.h"
@@ -703,3 +708,5 @@
         }
     }
 }  // namespace Ogre
+
+#endif  // !OGRE_NO_FREEIMAGE
